   "definition_of_done": [
    "Green output is logic HIGH if and only if the 4-bit input (a,b,c,d) encodes 5 (0101), 6 (0110), 12 (1100), or 13 (1101).",
    "Red output is logic HIGH if and only if the 4-bit input encodes 1 (0001), 2 (0010), 3 (0011), or 4 (0100).",
    "For all remaining 8 input combinations (0,7,8,9,10,11,14,15), both green and red outputs are logic LOW.",
    "All 16 input combinations produce stable, deterministic outputs with no floating or undefined states in ideal simulation.",
    "Total gate count consists of at most 19 two-input NAND gates (NOT gates count as NAND with tied inputs).",
    "Every gate in the blueprint has a unique name, a valid type (NAND or NOT), exactly 1 or 2 inputs, and 1 output, and every output nets to a real signal.",
    "Primary inputs a, b, c, d are connected to all sub-parts requiring them, and all outputs are driven under every input condition."
   ]
